
  [1mB. Store + granular DOM patching[0m
  Same store, but the view diffs and updates only the affected [38;5;153m<li>[39m. Faster and preserves focus/scroll naturally. Cost:
  you hand-write the reconciliation that a framework would give you, which is exactly the code that accumulates subtle
  bugs. Premature for a personal task list.

  [1mC. No store — handlers read/write localStorage directly[0m
  Least code today. But there's no single place where "a task changed" happens, which is precisely the seam the
  notification system needs next. This one actively undermines sub-project 2.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. The store-emits-change seam is the whole reason to pick an architecture now rather than later: the
  reminder engine becomes a subscriber, not a rewrite. If the list ever gets big enough for re-rendering to hurt, A
  upgrades to B without touching the store.

  Assuming A, here's the [1mmodule structure[0m — first design section:

  - [38;5;153msrc/store.js[39m — task CRUD, validation, id generation, emits [38;5;153mchange[39m. Takes a storage object as a constructor arg (real
    [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m in the app, a fake in tests). No DOM.
  - [38;5;153msrc/storage.js[39m — localStorage read/write, JSON serialization, a schema version field, and graceful handling of
    corrupt or absent data.
  - [38;5;153msrc/view.js[39m — renders the list and form from store state, translates DOM events into store calls. No business logic.
  - [38;5;153msrc/main.js[39m — wires the three together.
  - [38;5;153mindex.html[39m — loads [38;5;153mmain.js[39m as a module.

  The boundary that matters: [38;5;153mstore.js[39m has no DOM and [38;5;153mview.js[39m has no storage. That keeps the logic testable headlessly
  and gives the reminder engine a clean thing to attach to.

  Two notes on things I'd handle explicitly rather than leave implicit: [1mdates[0m are stored as ISO-8601 UTC strings and
  only formatted for display at the view layer, and [1mcorrupt localStorage[0m falls back to an empty list with a visible
  warning rather than throwing on boot — the schema version field is there so sub-project 2 can migrate the shape when
  it adds reminder state.

  Does the module split look right before I go on to the UI behavior and testing sections?

